<title>TURKEY: TURK YAPI KREDI BANK 9-MTH PROFITS JUMP.</title>
<headline>TURK YAPI KREDI BANK 9-MTH PROFITS JUMP.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1996-11-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jan-Sept 1996 provisional</p>
<p>(billion lira unless stated)</p>
<p>    Per share profit (lira)	  475.12  vs     560.81</p>
<p>    Net profit			12,248.43  vs   4,663.71</p>
<p>    Net interest income	   23,392.66  vs   7,053.14</p>
<p>    Net non-interest expense     8,848.56  vs   1,877.60</p>
<p>    Provisions for bad loans	 339.86  vs     258.57</p>
<p>    Loans			    220,567.00  vs  93,535.67</p>
<p>    Deposits			 336,485.65  vs 145,614.94</p>
<p>    Loans borrowed		   8,721.71  vs   5,726.65</p>
<p>    Equity			    40,121.18  vs  15,457.97</p>
<p>    Capital			   25,779.60  vs   8,316.00</p>
<p>NOTE - Yapi Kredi Bankasi A.S., a leading Turkish commercial bank, is largely owned by financial and industrial group Cukurova.</p>
<p>Figures above do not take into account Turkey's 79.3 percent year-on-year consumer price inflation in September.</p>
<p>-- Istanbul newsroom +90-212-2750875</p>
</text>
